WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
FloodHUB, in use. A full run of the flood-risk tool on one basin. Waiting time is cut and some steps are sped up.

2
00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:08.520
Khola, the FloodHUB tool. Running locally in Docker [1.6x speed]

3
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:14.280
Step 1 of 8: Area of interest. A HydroBASINS level 8 basin containing the Kathmandu Valley

4
00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:21.120
Step 2 of 8: Criteria. Eleven factors, each reclassified from 1 to 5 [2x speed]

5
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:26.440
Step 3 of 8: Weighting. Equal weights in this session [1.4x speed]

6
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:35.760
Step 4 of 8: Compute. Criteria combined into a risk surface

7
00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:41.760
Step 5 of 8: Vulnerability report. Every building in the basin is tagged with a hazard class

8
00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:54.920
Step 5 of 8: Vulnerability report. Area, people and buildings per hazard class (67 s of processing cut)

9
00:00:54.700 --> 00:01:07.000
Step 6 of 8: Validate. Against flood incidents recorded on the BIPAD Portal, 2011 to 2026 [1.25x speed]

10
00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:17.800
Step 7 of 8: Compare to METEOR. Agreement with a modelled 1-in-100-year river flood [1.25x speed]

11
00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:24.300
Equal weights and the app's default class breaks: an illustration of the pipeline, not a validated assessment. Step 8, shelter siting, is left out because it maps individual buildings.
